                                                "sense_id": "f370b50e-0c74-325c-9965-0b80da6571a1",
                                                "text": "I put in an extra hour at work today."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eb222daa-3abf-4466-be4e-6c0a91a0e42b",
                                                "sense_id": "f370b50e-0c74-325c-9965-0b80da6571a1",
                                                "text": "Despite his success, the comedian liked to put in appearances at some of the smaller venues."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b5ddb008-e4dd-3fbc-bce5-429a89f7f72e",
                                        "entry_id": "68773aaf-c390-3fb3-b4ec-76d8d5e27805",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To call at (a place or port), especially as a deviation from an intended journey."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated",
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c29ff061-36d7-4969-b1c9-87e96335f339",
                                                "sense_id": "b5ddb008-e4dd-3fbc-bce5-429a89f7f72e",
                                                "text": "We put in at Brixham, a most excellent fishing Town, but very dirty and disagreeable."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1c5304cd-dc23-45ff-94f0-0bb490733719",
                                                "sense_id": "b5ddb008-e4dd-3fbc-bce5-429a89f7f72e",
                                                "text": "“They were bound for Quebec—hadn’t any notion of coming to P. E. I. They had a long rough voyage and water got scarce, so the captain of the New Moon put in here to get some."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2f801b41-22f4-37ba-aef5-a56d27977c58",
